      },
      "message": "fix(post): Fanuc-family mill posts state the clearance Z before the first X/Y traverse\n\nfanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm, sinumerik and heidenhain wrote the first\nmove after a tool change as one combined rapid (G00 X20 Y10 Z-3) from\nwherever the change left the tip - a straight line through the part when a\nlong tool on a high work offset stands below the part top (the #1614\nhazard). At the program's start and after every tool change the first\nmotion now starts with a Z-only rapid to the section's ClearancePlane, else\nits RetractPlane, never below the move's own Z, then X/Y alone at it (and,\nfor a feed, arc or probing move, a rapid down to its start). A first canned\ncycle is positioned over its hole at that height. A stream stating neither\nplane is refused by name with the #1618/#1632 wording.\n\nFrame: written after the record's own tilt(), so under G43.4 when the first\nrecord arms it (the tip's work-frame Z) and in G43 with the table clamped on\nDoosan's indexing path; the rotaries turn only on the record. Decision in\ndocs/decisions/1633-fanuc-first-traverse-clearance.md.\n\nPinned by crates/post/tests/first_traverse_clearance_fanuc_family.rs; 161\ngoldens gained only the inserted Z (and X/Y) rapids, checked by script.\n\nFixes #1633\nRefs #1616\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
