      "message": "fix(post): a refused first traverse writes no move; name what is taken on trust\n\nReview of PR #1636 (NeoTech):\n- after the no-plane refusal, xyFirst returns false and the six posts'\n  motion hooks write nothing for the move - nor for any later motion of\n  the section while X/Y stay unknown - so no combined G00 X Y Z from an\n  unknown height reaches the program text; the refusal pin now asserts\n  it for every post (mutation: putting the write back turns it red);\n- the decision file names what is taken on trust: the clearance plane\n  over the tool-change X/Y, G43.4 with an unknown rotary pose, the Doosan\n  index path; and that end-to-end blocking on a warning is the callers'.\n\nRefs #1633\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
